{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|apologie}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fr|apologie}}, from {{der|en|LL.|apologia}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἀπολογία||a speech in defence}}, from {{m|grc|ἀπολογοῦμαι||I speak in my defense}}, from {{m|grc|ἀπόλογος||an account, story}}, from {{m|grc|ἀπό||from, off}} (see ''[[apo-]]'') + {{m|grc|λόγος||speech}}. {{doublet|en|apologia}}. {{surf|en|apo|-logy}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/əˈpɒl.ə.d͡ʒi/}}
** {{rhymes|en|ɒlədʒi|s=4}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/əˈpɑ.lə.d͡ʒi/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-apology.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An expression of [[remorse]] or [[regret]] for having said or done something that [[harm]]ed another: an instance of [[apologize|apologizing]] (saying that one is [[sorry]]).
#: {{ux|en|What he said really hurt my feelings, but his '''apology''' sounded so sincere that I couldn't help but forgive him.}}
#: {{ux|en|The CEO made a public '''apology''' for the scandal, and promised full cooperation with the authorities.}}
# A formal [[justification]], [[defence]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''Apology''' of Socrates.}}
#: {{syn|en|apologia}}
# Anything provided as a [[substitute]]; a [[makeshift]].
#: {{ux|en|a poor '''apology''' for a hotel room}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Bleak House|20}}
#*: [He] goes to work devising '''apologies''' for window curtains.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1947|month=January and February|author=Cecil J. Allen|title=British Locomotive Practice and Performance|journal=Railway Magazine|page=39|text=The response to firing is remarkable, and though the 280 lb. pressure seems more in the nature of a reserve for emergencies than a continuous working figure, even with the present-day '''apology''' for coal it seldom fell below 250 lb., and could always be brought up to blowing-off point with little difficulty. To this liveliness of steaming the thermic syphons are doubtless the chief contributory.}}

